## Summary of the customerCode / checkDigit feature

The `customerCode` feature is fully implemented; `checkDigit` is currently referenced **only in the test** (which fails until you add the field). The DTOs are generated at build time from `openapi.yml` via the OpenAPI Generator Maven plugin, so `checkDigit` must be added to the OpenAPI schema and populated through the `OwnerMapper`.

### 1. Every file mentioning `customerCode` / `checkDigit`

**Main source:**

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` — generates the code. Format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:
  ```java
  owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", cityPrefix, lastPrefix, sequence));
  ```
  `cityPrefix`/`lastPrefix` = upper-cased first 3 letters of city / lastName; `sequence` = (count of existing owners in that city) + 1, zero-padded to 4. Example `SYD-SMI-0007`.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MembershipNumber.java` — derives `membershipNumber` from `customerCode` + `registrationDate` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`). Returns null if either is null.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` — logs `customerCode` in the AUDIT log line.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — the entity. Field at lines 60-61 with getter/setter (123-129):
  ```java
  @Column(name = "customer_code")
  private String customerCode;
  public String getCustomerCode() { return this.customerCode; }
  public void setCustomerCode(String customerCode) { this.customerCode = customerCode; }
  ```

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — maps `customerCode` (inherited from OwnerFields) plus derived fields. Lines 29-30 add `membershipNumber` via an expression using `getCustomerCode()`. This is where a `checkDigit` mapping would be added.

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — schema. Lines 2094-2099 define `customerCode`; lines 2100-2105 define `membershipNumber`. **No `checkDigit` property exists yet.**

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — pipeline; step `customerCode` (lines 32-34) runs `AssignCustomerCode`.

**Test source:**

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the only reference to `checkDigit` (see below).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — provides the `luhn(...)` helper.

### 2. Test expectations (expected checkDigit value)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`:
```java
/** check-digit: 'checkDigit' is the Luhn check digit over the digits of the customerCode. */
@Test
void coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode() throws Exception {
    JsonNode r = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(ownerNode()));
    assertEquals(luhn(r.get("customerCode").asText()), r.get("checkDigit").asInt());
}
```
The expected value is **not a literal** — it is recomputed at runtime by `luhn(customerCode)`. `checkDigit` must be an **integer** JSON field on the owner GET/response body.

The exact Luhn algorithm the test uses (`AcceptanceBase.java` lines 301-321) — this is the spec your production code must replicate:
```java
protected static int luhn(String s) {
    int sum = 0;
    boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = s.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') continue;   // skip non-digits (the dashes/letters)
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) d -= 9; }
        sum += d;
        dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```
Note it starts with `dbl = true` from the rightmost digit and ignores non-digit characters, so for `SYD-SMI-0007` it operates on the digits `0007`.

The test flow: `createOwnerOk(ownerNode())` POSTs a valid owner and returns its id; `fetchOwner(id)` GETs `/api/owners/{id}` and returns the JSON body. So `checkDigit` must appear on the **GET owner response**, not only the create response.

### 3. DTO / response structure where checkDigit should be added

The DTOs are **generated**, not hand-written. Per `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (lines 369-411), the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` generates model classes from `openapi.yml` with `modelNameSuffix=Dto` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`. So `OwnerDto` is produced from the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`.

The `Owner` schema (openapi.yml, from line ~2069) is `allOf: [OwnerFields, {id, displayName, initials, customerCode, membershipNumber, householdId, identityKey, namesakeCount, membershipLevel, locality, bulkSignupWarning, contactPreference, pets}]`. `customerCode` lives here (lines 2094-2099) as a read-only string. A new `checkDigit` property would be added alongside these derived read-only fields, e.g.:
```yaml
checkDigit:
  type: integer
  format: int32
  readOnly: true
```

The response is built in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`:
```java
OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
response.send(ResponseEntity.created(...).body(dto));
```
And the GET path uses `RespondWithOwner` (referenced in the GET yml). Both go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`. Since `checkDigit` is a derived value (not stored on `Owner`), the natural place to populate it is a new `@Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "...")` in `OwnerMapper.java` (mirroring the existing `membershipNumber` mapping at lines 29-30), computing Luhn over `owner.getCustomerCode()`. There is currently no Luhn utility class in main source — only the test has one — so a production helper would need to be created (e.g. a `CheckDigit`/`Luhn` class in the `rest.function.owner` package, matching the pattern of `MembershipNumber`).

### 4. OfficeFloor YAML endpoints for customer/owner and their function classes

Directory `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`:

- `owners.POST.yml` — create pipeline. Ordered steps → function classes (all in `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`):
  `RequireOwnerFields` → `RequirePostcode` → `RequireUniqueIdentity` → `RequireCityCapacity` → `RequireDailyRegistrationLimit` → `BuildOwner` → **`AssignCustomerCode`** → `CountNamesakes` → `CountHouseholdMembers` → `FlagBulkSignupWarning` → `SaveOwner` → `AuditOwnerCreated` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`.
- `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` — `LoadOwner` → `RespondWithOwner`. (This is the path the test's `fetchOwner` hits.)
- `owners.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}/pets.POST.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}.PUT.yml`, `.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}/visits.POST.yml`, and `api/v2/owners.GET.yml`.

Function classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` and `RespondWithOwner` are the response builders; both call `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`.

### 5. Running the tests

- Build tool: **Maven**. Wrapper present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`), config under `/home/daniel/sandbox/.mvn`. No Gradle wrapper (`gradlew` absent; only `pom.xml`).
- Run the full suite: `./mvnw test` (or `./mvnw verify`). Run just this test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- Note: `./mvnw` will also run the `openapi-generator` `generate` goal (bound to `generate-sources`) and MapStruct annotation processing, so any `openapi.yml` schema change to add `checkDigit` is picked up automatically on the next build. The readme (`/home/daniel/sandbox/readme.md`, line 25) documents `./mvnw spring-boot:run` for running the app.

